{
 "format": 1,
 "note": "PRISM M3: the Covenant's and the Marines' overlay assignments (Tier 0: shader names, class names and channel rules only). overlay_pack.py merges them into overlay.json (shaders as overlay.json's, uv_wu filled in from measure_uv_density.py). Two classes a shader (the renderer's v1 rule: slot A above the multipurpose channel's hi, slot B below lo); the finer splits (Elite suit vs skin, Marine hands, boots, metal) are in class_mask_recipes_m3.json for the class masks. Thresholds measured on the extracted maps (material_masks.py): Covenant b is the change-colour plate (clean), Jackal and Marine r is 0 on cloth and 0.1-0.7 noisy on plates (a narrow step at 0.05-0.15, not a weight), face b is graded skin vs hair on a 32x32 map (a soft step 0.2-0.55). g above 0.1 is self-illumination: left alone. null: no overlay (lights, eyes, emblems, shields, teeth). uv_wu: measured on the player's own maps (measure_uv_density.py, b30 then a50: overlay_pack.py's --uv JSONs). r4: where class_mask_recipes_m3.json's classes all exist (the Marines' hands to human_skin and boots to hard_polymer, the Jackal's feet to skin_jackal) the shader names its class mask (class_masks.py, built locally into prism_class_masks) and the recipe's slots; without the mask the renderer falls back to the two-class channel rule (slot B below lo), as before. The Elite's cov_bodysuit and the Marine torso's marine_metal still have no mask.",
 "aliases": {
  "skin_grunt_half": {
   "of": "skin_grunt",
   "normal": 0.5,
   "cavity": 0.5,
   "rough": 0.5,
   "note": "CE's grunt detail map (x12, mask 5 = 1 - change colour) already lies on the skin of grunt torso and grunt arms and legs: our skin at half strength there"
  }
 },
